/* 
Page Object Model (POM) follows the Encapsulation concept.
Encapsulation means wrapping data (locators/properties)
and methods (actions) into a single class.

Variables/properties are marked as:
- private   → cannot be accessed outside the class
- readonly  → values will not change after initialization

When an object of the class is created, the constructor gets invoked automatically.

The Playwright page fixture is passed to the constructor, which initializes the page object 
and helps locate elements.

Action methods are created for all locators to perform reusable operations on the page.
*/